  "scenes": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "tag": "System design",
      "heading": "Why does your report return *504*?",
      "narration": "You export the yearly sales report: fifty million rows. It takes minutes. And right at the one-minute mark, the user gets a 504 error. Why, if your code didn't fail?",
      "beats": [
        {
          "text": "Sales",
          "icon": "db",
          "at": "yearly sales report"
        },
        {
          "text": "Minutes",
          "icon": "scheduler",
          "at": "It takes minutes",
          "sfx": "clock"
        },
        {
          "text": "504",
          "at": "a 504 error",
          "sfx": "impact"
        },
        {
          "text": "?",
          "at": "if your code"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "board",
      "title": "What your diagram doesn't show",
      "narration": "Your diagram has a frontend, a backend and a database. But between the frontend and your API there's almost always a middleman: your hosting, Cloudflare or nginx. It's called a proxy.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": "Your diagram has",
          "show": [
            "frontend",
            "api",
            "db"
          ],
          "camera": []
        },
        {
          "at": "almost always a",
          "show": [
            "proxy"
          ],
          "hide": [
            "frontend->api"
          ],
          "focus": [
            "frontend",
            "proxy",
            "api"
          ],
          "sfx": "impact"
        },
        {
          "at": "Cloudflare or nginx",
          "packet": {
            "from": "frontend",
            "to": "api",
            "via": [
              "proxy"
            ],
            "label": "HTTPS",
            "color": "blue"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "called a proxy",
          "focus": [
            "proxy"
          ],
          "note": {
            "text": "It's there even if *you didn't add it*",
            "tone": "warn"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "board",
      "title": "What breaks",
      "narration": "And a proxy doesn't wait forever. If the connection stays silent for a minute or two, it cuts it. Error 504: the proxy got tired of waiting.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": "doesn't wait forever",
          "focus": [
            "frontend",
            "proxy",
            "api",
            "db"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": "a minute or two",
          "packet": {
            "from": "api",
            "to": "db",
            "label": "slow query",
            "color": "yellow"
          },
          "status": {
            "frontend": "busy",
            "api": "busy",
            "db": "busy"
          },
          "note": {
            "text": "nginx *60 s* · Cloudflare *100 s*",
            "tone": "warn"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "Error 504",
          "status": {
            "proxy": "error",
            "frontend": "error"
          },
          "packet": {
            "from": "proxy",
            "to": "frontend",
            "label": "504",
            "color": "red"
          },
          "sfx": "riser"
        },
        {
          "at": "got tired of waiting",
          "note": {
            "text": "504 = the proxy *got tired of waiting*",
            "tone": "bad"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "board",
      "title": "What if I raise the timeout?",
      "narration": "So, raise the timeout? Your server stays busy for minutes, and if the user closes the tab, all that work is lost. The problem is waiting on the same connection.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": "raise the timeout",
          "status": {
            "proxy": "idle",
            "frontend": "idle"
          },
          "focus": [
            "proxy"
          ],
          "note": {
            "text": "A *10-minute* timeout?",
            "tone": "info"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "stays busy for minutes",
          "focus": [
            "api",
            "db"
          ],
          "status": {
            "api": "busy"
          },
          "sfx": "cash"
        },
        {
          "at": "closes the tab",
          "focus": [
            "frontend",
            "api"
          ],
          "status": {
            "frontend": "warn",
            "api": "warn"
          },
          "note": {
            "text": "Tab closed → *work lost*",
            "tone": "bad"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "The problem is",
          "focus": [],
          "camera": [],
          "note": {
            "text": "The problem: *waiting on the same connection*",
            "tone": "warn"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "board",
      "title": "The way out",
      "narration": "The way out: the API answers right away with a 202, received but not ready, and builds the report separately. I'll show you how in the next short.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": "The way out",
          "status": {
            "frontend": "idle",
            "proxy": "idle",
            "api": "idle",
            "db": "idle"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "answers right away",
          "hide": [
            "api->db"
          ],
          "packet": {
            "from": "api",
            "to": "frontend",
            "via": [
              "proxy"
            ],
            "label": "202 + jobId",
            "color": "green"
          },
          "status": {
            "frontend": "ok"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "received but not",
          "note": {
            "text": "*202* = received, not ready yet",
            "tone": "good"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "builds the report separately",
          "note": {
            "text": "Heavy work, *separately*",
            "tone": "good"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "summary",
      "title": "Remember",
      "narration": "Remember: a 504 isn't your code, it's a proxy that got tired of waiting. Has it happened to you? The full design, step by step, is on the channel.",
      "points": [
        {
          "text": "504 = a proxy *got tired of waiting*",
          "at": "a 504 isn't"
        },
        {
          "text": "Slow work: *answer 202* and do it separately",
          "at": "got tired of waiting"
        }
      ],
      "cta": "Full video on the channel ▶"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Default timeouts: nginx proxy_read_timeout 60 s; AWS ALB idle timeout 60 s (configurable up to 4000 s); Cloudflare 100 s (returns 524, not 504); API Gateway REST historically 29 s.",
    "The 504 comes from the middleman (Gateway Timeout), not your app: your backend may keep working after the user already got the error.",
    "Raising the timeout is fine for something just over the limit, but it doesn't scale: it ties up connections and server workers, and it doesn't survive the user closing the tab."
  ],
